What is a Dust‑free and Oxygen‑free Oven?
Dust‑free and Oxygen‑free Ovens are engineered to eliminate both particulate contamination and oxidative exposure during thermal processing. By continuously circulating inert gas and using high‑efficiency filtration, they create an environment where oxygen levels are kept at sub‑10 ppm and airborne particles are reduced to fewer than 100 particles ≥ 0.5 µm per cubic foot (Class 100). Such stringent conditions are essential for processes where trace oxygen or dust can degrade product performance, cause yield losses, or trigger regulatory non‑compliance.
